WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.123 --> 00:00:02.827
- No matter who you are, no
matter where you are in life,

00:00:02.827 --> 00:00:05.230
you can take the lid off of your job.

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:08.182
There is nothing bigger than your dream.

00:00:08.182 --> 00:00:11.944
It's going to take more than
a notion to become successful.

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:15.241
Like I always say, life is
10% what happens to you.

00:00:15.241 --> 00:00:17.830
It's 90% what you do about it.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:22.068
And you got to prep and
plan, and plan, and plan.

00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:24.990
Extend yourself beyond your
normal levels of comfort.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.710
And buy your first class ticket.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:29.194
- Hello, Believe Nation,
I'm Evan Carmichael.

00:00:29.194 --> 00:00:30.714
My one word is believe.

00:00:30.714 --> 00:00:32.886
And I believe that
entrepreneurs are going to solve

00:00:32.886 --> 00:00:34.790
all of the world's major problems.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.702
So to help you on your journey, today,

00:00:36.702 --> 00:00:39.324
we're going to learn from
comedian, TV host and actor,

00:00:39.324 --> 00:00:42.844
Steve Harvey, and my take on
his Top 10 rules for Success,

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:44.444
Volume two.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.900
Rule number one is my personal favorite.

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.153
And I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:48.153 --> 00:00:49.742
And as always, as you're listening,

00:00:49.742 --> 00:00:51.403
if something really resonates with you,

00:00:51.403 --> 00:00:53.260
if there's a message that
really holds true to you,

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:55.304
please leave it down in the comments below

00:00:55.304 --> 00:00:58.137
and put it in quotes so that
other people can be inspired.

00:00:58.137 --> 00:01:00.715
And when you write it down,
it's much more likely to stick

00:01:00.715 --> 00:01:01.898
with yourself as well.

00:01:01.898 --> 00:01:02.731
Enjoy.

00:01:06.745 --> 00:01:09.495
(powerful music)

00:01:15.939 --> 00:01:19.261
- No matter who you are, no
matter where you are in life,

00:01:19.261 --> 00:01:21.595
you can take the lid off of your job.

00:01:21.595 --> 00:01:26.250
And if you're wondering
if you still have the lid

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.746
on in your life, here are some clues

00:01:28.746 --> 00:01:31.890
that's going to let you know
that the lid is still on.

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.781
If you're not excited about
waking up in the morning,

00:01:34.781 --> 00:01:38.394
if you're sitting around
bored out of your mind,

00:01:38.394 --> 00:01:43.247
if you've got time to do
everything anybody asks you to do,

00:01:43.247 --> 00:01:45.854
(audience laughing)

00:01:45.854 --> 00:01:47.241
you probably got the lid on.

00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:51.049
If when you tell your
dreams to all your friends

00:01:51.049 --> 00:01:55.472
it makes sense to them,
you got your lid on, man.

00:01:55.472 --> 00:01:58.584
Your dreams should not
make sense to everybody.

00:01:58.584 --> 00:02:00.765
You got to say something
that make people go,

00:02:00.765 --> 00:02:01.869
"How you going to do that?'

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:03.855
That's when you got the lid off.

00:02:03.855 --> 00:02:06.328
And if I were you, I'd do
that, I'd take the lid off.

00:02:06.328 --> 00:02:08.429
Make sense to me, darnit.
(audience laughing)

00:02:08.429 --> 00:02:11.950
The one thing that I have learned to relay

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:13.888
to all of my children

00:02:13.888 --> 00:02:14.888
is to dream.

00:02:16.908 --> 00:02:19.580
There is nothing bigger than your dream.

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:22.528
Nothing is greater than your dream.

00:02:22.528 --> 00:02:27.148
Now as we sit in this great
educational institution,

00:02:27.148 --> 00:02:30.525
I am not saying that your
education is not important,

00:02:30.525 --> 00:02:33.357
because it's tied to a lot of your dreams,

00:02:33.357 --> 00:02:35.148
but let me tell you something.

00:02:35.148 --> 00:02:39.097
There ain't nothing, nothing,
bigger than your dream,

00:02:39.097 --> 00:02:43.343
because your dream will propel
you to get the education.

00:02:43.343 --> 00:02:45.227
Don't you ever stop dreaming.

00:02:45.227 --> 00:02:47.727
Don't you ever stop imagining.

00:02:48.617 --> 00:02:50.672
Oh, we're going to talk
about them two things a lot.

00:02:50.672 --> 00:02:52.843
But don't you ever stop dreaming.

00:02:52.843 --> 00:02:56.686
Your Bible says a man
without a dream or vision

00:02:56.686 --> 00:02:57.684
shall perish.

00:02:57.684 --> 00:02:59.019
That's in your Bible.

00:02:59.019 --> 00:03:00.384
It ain't just in the one I read.

00:03:00.384 --> 00:03:04.511
No where in there does it say
without education you perish.

00:03:04.511 --> 00:03:07.598
But it says without a dream
or vision, you perish.

00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:11.765
So if what you are dreaming
about requires an education,

00:03:13.728 --> 00:03:17.230
it is then your dream that
propels you to get the education.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:20.158
But the dream is bigger
than everything, man.

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:22.432
See, if it was an education

00:03:22.432 --> 00:03:24.672
that caused you to be great or successful.

00:03:24.672 --> 00:03:28.520
I ain't here today, 'cause
I don't have one of them.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.937
But nobody could outdream me.

00:03:32.444 --> 00:03:35.741
Your dream is everything, man.

00:03:35.741 --> 00:03:37.329
It's the biggest part of your life.

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:41.036
(audience laughing)
(laughs) Look man,

00:03:41.036 --> 00:03:43.613
it is that thing that God puts in you

00:03:43.613 --> 00:03:45.900
that don't let you sleep sometime.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.085
It's your dream.

00:03:47.085 --> 00:03:49.035
It's that thing that part of you, man,

00:03:49.035 --> 00:03:52.297
that wakes you up and stirs
the very pit of your soul.

00:03:52.297 --> 00:03:55.630
I've always taught my children to dream.

00:03:57.807 --> 00:04:01.818
The secret, though, the
secret to real success

00:04:01.818 --> 00:04:04.767
is if you tie your gift to the dream.

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:08.593
It's going to take more than
a notion to become successful.

00:04:08.593 --> 00:04:12.684
'Cause one you get this
degree, it's actually

00:04:12.684 --> 00:04:14.972
just going to be a piece of
paper on the paper on the wall.

00:04:14.972 --> 00:04:17.673
That's really all it's going to be.

00:04:17.673 --> 00:04:19.384
Some people may give you a job with it.

00:04:19.384 --> 00:04:21.065
The majority of people going to tell you

00:04:21.065 --> 00:04:22.283
how much experience you need.

00:04:22.283 --> 00:04:23.749
So you got to hustle, man.

00:04:23.749 --> 00:04:25.316
Got to hustle.

00:04:25.316 --> 00:04:27.566
Hustle and grind, dig, man.

00:04:28.543 --> 00:04:31.121
Got to fight, you've got to
have a lot of dog in you,

00:04:31.121 --> 00:04:32.197
man, to be rich.

00:04:32.197 --> 00:04:35.042
Now if you just want a job,
get yourself a little job,

00:04:35.042 --> 00:04:37.990
create some nice, little
life, get a little house,

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.105
some grandkids.

00:04:39.105 --> 00:04:41.602
(audience laughing)
(drowned by laughter)

00:04:41.602 --> 00:04:43.601
Get yourself a little
minivan, a station wagon,

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:46.050
go on and ride your life out,
ain't nothing wrong with that.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:50.217
But if you really, really,
really want to be bolder,

00:04:52.288 --> 00:04:57.106
change some people's lives,
get yourselves some real money,

00:04:57.106 --> 00:04:58.104
hire people.

00:04:58.104 --> 00:05:01.227
Get more than one stream
of income coming in,

00:05:01.227 --> 00:05:02.911
got to be hustlin', man.

00:05:02.911 --> 00:05:05.326
You got to be a hustler.

00:05:05.326 --> 00:05:06.833
You all in the tank.

00:05:06.833 --> 00:05:08.495
That shit is money, man.

00:05:08.495 --> 00:05:10.688
(audience laughing)

00:05:10.688 --> 00:05:13.499
Money can't buy you happiness,
they ass don't have no money.

00:05:13.499 --> 00:05:15.168
(audience laughing)

00:05:15.168 --> 00:05:17.558
Let me tell you what, you go be poets,

00:05:17.558 --> 00:05:19.025
see how that work out.

00:05:19.025 --> 00:05:20.686
I lived in a car for three years, man.

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:21.731
I struggled.

00:05:21.731 --> 00:05:23.356
But I had a dream and a vision.

00:05:23.356 --> 00:05:25.666
When I got there, I hustle, man.

00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:26.932
I hustle.

00:05:26.932 --> 00:05:30.097
Every man in this room, you blew your 20s.

00:05:30.097 --> 00:05:33.515
You spent all your 30s tryin'
to make up for your 20s.

00:05:33.515 --> 00:05:35.104
- Yep, that's the truth.

00:05:35.104 --> 00:05:39.308
- Dog, every dude in
this room blew they 20s

00:05:39.308 --> 00:05:43.986
and at 30 tryin' to fix what they
should have did in their 20s.

00:05:43.986 --> 00:05:45.992
And so far it's on.

00:05:45.992 --> 00:05:48.828
You turn 40, you're trying
to recover from the mistakes

00:05:48.828 --> 00:05:50.013
you made when you 30.

00:05:50.013 --> 00:05:52.032
Now at 40, man, it's
time for you to start.

00:05:52.032 --> 00:05:55.375
Really, at 30 you need to
start bucklin' it on down.

00:05:55.375 --> 00:05:58.290
And just realize, man,
everybody make mistakes.

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.044
And the mistakes you going through

00:06:00.044 --> 00:06:02.702
are going to help you become the person

00:06:02.702 --> 00:06:03.781
you need to be later on.

00:06:03.781 --> 00:06:04.780
- Steve Harvey.

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.311
- All them mistakes,
dog, they cool to make.

00:06:07.311 --> 00:06:09.680
I needed to mess up every marriage.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.513
I need to get arrested like I did.

00:06:13.683 --> 00:06:15.537
I needed to get shot.

00:06:15.537 --> 00:06:17.760
I needed all this, dog.

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:19.565
- You got shot?
- I needed to be home.

00:06:19.565 --> 00:06:21.363
Yeah, let's not bring that up.

00:06:21.363 --> 00:06:23.051
(host laughing)

00:06:23.051 --> 00:06:24.897
Because all them people
that be talkin' about,

00:06:24.897 --> 00:06:27.263
"Man, you get shot, it
don't hurt it just burn."

00:06:27.263 --> 00:06:29.355
That's a complete lie.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:31.341
(others laughing)

00:06:31.341 --> 00:06:32.558
Pow! (screaming)

00:06:32.558 --> 00:06:36.124
Oh, Jesus, Jesus!
(gunshots exploding)

00:06:36.124 --> 00:06:37.970
I'm telling you, shot ain't what you want.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.118
- Shot aint cool. (laughs)

00:06:39.118 --> 00:06:41.534
- I needed all them things to happen

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.821
to turn me into who I am today.

00:06:43.821 --> 00:06:46.051
So when you're young
and you make mistakes,

00:06:46.051 --> 00:06:47.310
don't let 'em eat you up,

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:50.245
'cause everybody that done
made it done made 'em.

00:06:50.245 --> 00:06:52.384
You got to fail in order to win.

00:06:52.384 --> 00:06:54.253
Hey, look, man.

00:06:54.253 --> 00:06:56.192
To understand how to hit
the game when it's shot,

00:06:56.192 --> 00:06:58.290
you got to miss the game when it's shot.

00:06:58.290 --> 00:06:59.381
- Steve Harvey (drowned by Steve).

00:06:59.381 --> 00:07:00.767
- You gots to miss 'em.

00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:03.454
- Well, I'm stuck in a
rut because I can't seem

00:07:03.454 --> 00:07:05.216
to follow through with anything.

00:07:05.216 --> 00:07:09.350
I went to college for a
year-and-a-half and I dropped out.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:11.033
Then I went to cosmetology school.

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:13.797
I completed that, but I never
went back to get my license.

00:07:13.797 --> 00:07:15.975
Then I was a pharmacy technician.

00:07:15.975 --> 00:07:18.998
And I recently let that
license expire as well.

00:07:18.998 --> 00:07:21.715
I just see so many people that are my age,

00:07:21.715 --> 00:07:23.768
and they're already set in their careers.

00:07:23.768 --> 00:07:27.191
And I just feel like at
29, I'm a people person,

00:07:27.191 --> 00:07:31.639
so I want to do something
like human resources

00:07:31.639 --> 00:07:33.765
and I just need help.

00:07:33.765 --> 00:07:35.345
Like where do I begin?

00:07:35.345 --> 00:07:38.918
- First of all, you're talking about stuff

00:07:38.918 --> 00:07:42.392
that I can relate to, like
so many others can relate to.

00:07:42.392 --> 00:07:45.237
I mean, everybody got the same story,

00:07:45.237 --> 00:07:47.148
we just got different details.

00:07:47.148 --> 00:07:50.773
But like I always say, life
is 10% what happens to you.

00:07:50.773 --> 00:07:53.608
It's 90% what you do about it.

00:07:53.608 --> 00:07:56.902
See, we're going to dive into
a chapter from my new book.

00:07:56.902 --> 00:07:58.711
And it's chapter one, section one.

00:07:58.711 --> 00:08:00.690
This is very clear for people.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:04.869
So the first step is getting
completely and brutally honest

00:08:04.869 --> 00:08:08.468
enough to say, "I am tired of myself."

00:08:08.468 --> 00:08:12.497
When you say, "I'm sick and
tired of being sick and tired."

00:08:12.497 --> 00:08:15.144
That's the facilitator of change.

00:08:15.144 --> 00:08:17.269
That's when you're ready
to say these words,

00:08:17.269 --> 00:08:19.157
"No more excuses."

00:08:19.157 --> 00:08:20.490
No more excuses.

00:08:21.762 --> 00:08:24.513
I went to Kent State, I dropped out.

00:08:24.513 --> 00:08:26.789
Well, I didn't drop out, I flunked out.

00:08:26.789 --> 00:08:28.948
Now that threw my life into a spiral,

00:08:28.948 --> 00:08:31.014
but because I didn't
have a college degree,

00:08:31.014 --> 00:08:33.302
I could not let that stop me.

00:08:33.302 --> 00:08:35.067
And like you're doing,
where you're saying,

00:08:35.067 --> 00:08:38.724
"All my friends at this age
are settled in their careers."

00:08:38.724 --> 00:08:40.594
You don't even know if
they're happy or not.

00:08:40.594 --> 00:08:43.623
Stop comparing yourself to others.

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:46.683
So the first thing you do is
stop focusing on other people.

00:08:46.683 --> 00:08:49.928
Instead, focus on being the best version

00:08:49.928 --> 00:08:51.703
of you that you can.

00:08:51.703 --> 00:08:54.165
Then you'll recognize
that you deserve to sit

00:08:54.165 --> 00:08:56.580
at the big table with everybody else

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:58.842
after you become the best that you can be.

00:08:58.842 --> 00:09:02.199
Now once you've accepted
that you have as much right

00:09:02.199 --> 00:09:05.137
to success and much right
to succeed as anybody else,

00:09:05.137 --> 00:09:07.689
the next step is learning
how to talk to talk.

00:09:07.689 --> 00:09:11.287
You have to get fluent in
the language of success

00:09:11.287 --> 00:09:13.252
so you speak it with ease.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.430
Surround yourself with people

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:17.234
who've accomplished their dreams.

00:09:17.234 --> 00:09:20.039
And immerse yourself in
the culture of achievement.

00:09:20.039 --> 00:09:22.622
I've learned if you're a farmer

00:09:25.239 --> 00:09:29.322
a farmer understands better
than any other worker

00:09:32.301 --> 00:09:34.289
in this country.

00:09:34.289 --> 00:09:38.456
A farmer has an understanding
that most people never achieve

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.628
in their life.

00:09:40.628 --> 00:09:45.063
I really respect the farmers
and their commitment.

00:09:45.063 --> 00:09:48.313
But I respect also their understanding.

00:09:50.863 --> 00:09:53.305
My grandfather and my uncle,

00:09:53.305 --> 00:09:57.138
the thing was to wake
up early in the morning,

00:10:01.533 --> 00:10:05.128
before you start your
day, you start your day

00:10:05.128 --> 00:10:08.235
by feeding all the animals.

00:10:08.235 --> 00:10:10.254
I never understood that.

00:10:10.254 --> 00:10:13.039
Why am I feeding slop to these hogs?

00:10:13.039 --> 00:10:15.756
Bailin' this hay for these cows,

00:10:15.756 --> 00:10:18.263
taking food out to the hunting dogs?

00:10:18.263 --> 00:10:20.794
Going to get these mules and horses,

00:10:20.794 --> 00:10:22.420
walkin' 'em down to water?

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:25.160
Why am I feeding these chickens, man?

00:10:25.160 --> 00:10:27.540
All this before I eat?

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.442
My grandfather says,
looked down at me, says,

00:10:30.442 --> 00:10:33.704
"Young man, if we don't
take care of these animals

00:10:33.704 --> 00:10:37.405
"that we are requiring
to take care of us,"

00:10:37.405 --> 00:10:39.975
he said, "what's going to happen to us?"

00:10:39.975 --> 00:10:43.911
He said, "We're depending on
them chickens to lay eggs,

00:10:43.911 --> 00:10:46.152
"to give us meat.

00:10:46.152 --> 00:10:48.903
"We're depending on them hogs for meet.

00:10:48.903 --> 00:10:51.465
"We're depending on the
mules to pull the plows

00:10:51.465 --> 00:10:52.792
"so we can plant.

00:10:52.792 --> 00:10:54.729
"We're depending on them horses

00:10:54.729 --> 00:10:57.124
"to drag all these wagons around.

00:10:57.124 --> 00:10:59.793
"We're dependent on these hunting dogs

00:10:59.793 --> 00:11:03.717
"to go out in the wood and
uncover the animals for."

00:11:03.717 --> 00:11:06.967
So then what I respect about farmers is

00:11:09.395 --> 00:11:13.250
they understand that
everything comes in seasons.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:15.500
There is a planting season.

00:11:16.501 --> 00:11:21.098
And you got to plant, and
plant, and plant, and plant,

00:11:21.098 --> 00:11:25.949
plow, till, hoe the rows,
you got to do all that,

00:11:25.949 --> 00:11:30.116
seed it, fertilize it, in
order for a crop to grow.

00:11:31.499 --> 00:11:34.581
Now here's what happens some years.

00:11:34.581 --> 00:11:38.748
Some years it's a drought,
ain't no rain, ain't no crops.

00:11:40.522 --> 00:11:45.178
Sometimes it's a flood,
wipe out all the crops,

00:11:45.178 --> 00:11:46.328
all the plants.

00:11:46.328 --> 00:11:47.745
But, guess what?

00:11:48.919 --> 00:11:51.067
You still got to do the planting,

00:11:51.067 --> 00:11:54.666
'cause what you're bankin'
on is just enough rain,

00:11:54.666 --> 00:11:58.312
just enough sunshine so you can harvest.

00:11:58.312 --> 00:12:02.479
And even the crops get washed
out, even if the floods come,

00:12:04.407 --> 00:12:07.867
even if the drought come,
the thing about a farmer,

00:12:07.867 --> 00:12:11.547
they do it all over again,
because they understand

00:12:11.547 --> 00:12:15.049
that eventually you'll be able to harvest.

00:12:15.049 --> 00:12:17.721
And that's what I respect about farmers.

00:12:17.721 --> 00:12:19.065
And that's my life.

00:12:19.065 --> 00:12:22.437
You know, you got to be tough
because the road to success

00:12:22.437 --> 00:12:24.153
is always under construction.

00:12:24.153 --> 00:12:27.302
It's never a clear path to success.

00:12:27.302 --> 00:12:30.633
The people who become successful
are the people who have

00:12:30.633 --> 00:12:32.397
a relentless attitude.

00:12:32.397 --> 00:12:36.729
And you just got to hang in
there through the bad breaks,

00:12:36.729 --> 00:12:38.443
'cause the bad breaks is comin',

00:12:38.443 --> 00:12:41.209
but they usually come
right before the big break

00:12:41.209 --> 00:12:42.427
is about to happen.

00:12:42.427 --> 00:12:44.415
You get a series of bad breaks

00:12:44.415 --> 00:12:46.214
and it stumbles up a lot of people.

00:12:46.214 --> 00:12:49.797
My life and my success
is to say to anyone,

00:12:51.242 --> 00:12:55.409
"You can stumble, you can fall,
you can get back up again."

00:12:57.358 --> 00:13:00.181
And like I've said before,
we each have a gift.

00:13:00.181 --> 00:13:04.683
But too many people miss
out because they refuse

00:13:04.683 --> 00:13:07.401
to sign the lease on their gift.

00:13:07.401 --> 00:13:11.032
You keep looking for it outside of you.

00:13:11.032 --> 00:13:13.657
Stop. Sit with yourself.

00:13:13.657 --> 00:13:15.368
What is it that you do the absolute best

00:13:15.368 --> 00:13:16.841
with the least amount of effort?

00:13:16.841 --> 00:13:17.852
That's your gift.

00:13:17.852 --> 00:13:21.946
But if you are constantly
looking outside of yourself

00:13:21.946 --> 00:13:24.233
and you don't latch onto your gift,

00:13:24.233 --> 00:13:26.234
you will never find your purpose.

00:13:26.234 --> 00:13:30.539
If you want to succeed, you
must commit to your own gift

00:13:30.539 --> 00:13:31.539
and embrace it.

00:13:31.539 --> 00:13:34.326
Knowledge is necessary to
get you to the next level.

00:13:34.326 --> 00:13:36.810
But after you get to the
next level, guess what?

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:38.991
All that's out the window.

00:13:38.991 --> 00:13:43.158
Geometry, history, all that's
out the window, man, sorry.

00:13:45.106 --> 00:13:46.112
You know?

00:13:46.112 --> 00:13:48.600
You got to learn this

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.853
and this can only be learned in life, man.

00:13:50.853 --> 00:13:53.159
With you all sitting up in
here catching first team

00:13:53.159 --> 00:13:57.326
is life lessons that you
could use when you're 58.

00:13:58.534 --> 00:13:59.815
You understand?

00:13:59.815 --> 00:14:03.621
You ain't going to, you
just can't get this,

00:14:03.621 --> 00:14:05.348
it's not available.

00:14:05.348 --> 00:14:06.765
You got to see it.

00:14:08.519 --> 00:14:11.077
So what you're actually doing is...

00:14:11.077 --> 00:14:13.781
See the thing about knowledge, man,

00:14:13.781 --> 00:14:15.429
you can Google knowledge.

00:14:15.429 --> 00:14:18.484
You could go online and
get knowledge on anything.

00:14:18.484 --> 00:14:22.393
You could press a button
and read about this

00:14:22.393 --> 00:14:23.495
and read about that.

00:14:23.495 --> 00:14:25.206
And you can go and repeat that.

00:14:25.206 --> 00:14:27.285
And people go, "Wow, he's knowledge."

00:14:27.285 --> 00:14:28.724
Okay, cool.

00:14:28.724 --> 00:14:32.997
But exposure, exposure
is totally different.

00:14:32.997 --> 00:14:36.851
Exposure is when you see it,
touch it, feel it, go there,

00:14:36.851 --> 00:14:37.850
experience.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:39.475
That's different.

00:14:39.475 --> 00:14:43.283
Exposure, once you open
your mind to exposure

00:14:43.283 --> 00:14:46.054
you can never shrink your mind back down.

00:14:46.054 --> 00:14:48.773
'Cause exposure don't decrease.

00:14:48.773 --> 00:14:51.445
Once you've been exposed and your mind

00:14:51.445 --> 00:14:55.575
expands from exposure, you
can't shrink it back down

00:14:55.575 --> 00:14:56.852
and act like it's okay.

00:14:56.852 --> 00:14:59.235
See, once you fly in first class,

00:14:59.235 --> 00:15:03.402
you can't walk past there
without feeling some kind of way

00:15:04.459 --> 00:15:06.677
and watch them people shut that curtain.

00:15:06.677 --> 00:15:07.683
You can't.

00:15:07.683 --> 00:15:10.378
'Cause the whole time you back there,

00:15:10.378 --> 00:15:13.202
see when I flew coach,
man, everywhere I went,

00:15:13.202 --> 00:15:14.950
'cause that's what I could afford to do.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:17.702
When the plane take off and
they close that curtain,

00:15:17.702 --> 00:15:19.332
the whole time I was wondering,

00:15:19.332 --> 00:15:21.329
what are they doing on the
other side of that curtain?

00:15:21.329 --> 00:15:24.441
Well, they're denying the exposure,

00:15:24.441 --> 00:15:27.064
because they can't show you.

00:15:27.064 --> 00:15:29.846
They can't show you watching them people

00:15:29.846 --> 00:15:32.243
get a whole can of coke.

00:15:32.243 --> 00:15:36.410
They can't show you that
they get their nuts warmed up

00:15:37.653 --> 00:15:38.657
in a container.

00:15:38.657 --> 00:15:41.607
They can't show you that
they give all them people

00:15:41.607 --> 00:15:43.963
a hot scented towel to
freshen their face and hands.

00:15:43.963 --> 00:15:48.130
They can't show that to you,
'cause you didn't pay for that.

00:15:49.158 --> 00:15:51.910
See, you bought the coach ticket.

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:53.462
So they closed the curtain.

00:15:53.462 --> 00:15:55.045
They don't even let you come up there

00:15:55.045 --> 00:15:56.298
and use their bathroom,

00:15:56.298 --> 00:15:59.941
because they just need to
keep these 10 seats available

00:15:59.941 --> 00:16:01.442
for those people that pay.

00:16:01.442 --> 00:16:02.725
That's what the curtains do.

00:16:02.725 --> 00:16:04.805
'Cause they know if they expose you to it,

00:16:04.805 --> 00:16:06.916
then you're going to want it.

00:16:06.916 --> 00:16:08.384
"Hey, I want a whole can of coke."

00:16:08.384 --> 00:16:10.358
"Well, we can't do that, you didn't pay."

00:16:10.358 --> 00:16:12.099
Or "I want some hot peanuts."

00:16:12.099 --> 00:16:13.632
No, no, no, no, no.

00:16:13.632 --> 00:16:15.894
Now on the airplanes, you got to pay.

00:16:15.894 --> 00:16:17.521
Now they done figured it out,

00:16:17.521 --> 00:16:18.996
you got to pay for the sandwich.

00:16:18.996 --> 00:16:21.620
You got to pay for the meal now.

00:16:21.620 --> 00:16:24.696
You get a choice, but
you get to buy it now.

00:16:24.696 --> 00:16:25.783
It's crazy.

00:16:25.783 --> 00:16:28.864
Your first class ticket
gets you a free food,

00:16:28.864 --> 00:16:32.097
gets you more than one bowl of nuts.

00:16:32.097 --> 00:16:33.952
You can get free drinks up there.

00:16:33.952 --> 00:16:37.089
You don't pay for beer
and drinks in first class.

00:16:37.089 --> 00:16:39.886
It comes with the cost of the ticket.

00:16:39.886 --> 00:16:42.732
So once you sit in first class

00:16:42.732 --> 00:16:45.583
and you open your mind and
expose your mind to it,

00:16:45.583 --> 00:16:49.040
see, bruh, you can't go
sit in coach no more,

00:16:49.040 --> 00:16:50.688
'cause you've been exposed.

00:16:50.688 --> 00:16:53.103
But if you keep walking past first class

00:16:53.103 --> 00:16:55.868
and let 'em close the curtain
and never get the experience,

00:16:55.868 --> 00:16:58.569
you can grow your whole
life thinking coach is fine

00:16:58.569 --> 00:17:02.240
But mess around and buy
yourself a first class ticket.

00:17:02.240 --> 00:17:04.749
You will forever be changed.

00:17:04.749 --> 00:17:07.520
And you will never forget
what first class was like.

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:09.250
But that's the beauty of exposure.

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:13.417
It makes you aim and perform
towards the exposure now.

00:17:15.164 --> 00:17:17.184
So that's why Dick Gregory said

00:17:17.184 --> 00:17:19.840
you should always, whenever
you can go first class,

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:22.571
extend yourself beyond your
normal levels of comfort,

00:17:22.571 --> 00:17:25.438
and buy your first class ticket.

00:17:25.438 --> 00:17:27.596
Get you a first class
suit, get you a first class

00:17:27.596 --> 00:17:28.598
pair of shoes.

00:17:28.598 --> 00:17:29.865
'Cause once you put it on,

00:17:29.865 --> 00:17:31.883
you understand what they're charging.

00:17:31.883 --> 00:17:33.961
And now you are forever changed,

00:17:33.961 --> 00:17:37.365
because through exposure your
mind cannot shrink back down.

00:17:37.365 --> 00:17:39.448
Knowledge, you can forget

00:17:40.488 --> 00:17:42.360
when Christopher discovered America.

00:17:42.360 --> 00:17:45.777
You can forget that equation for gravity.

00:17:48.151 --> 00:17:52.306
You can forget MC squared,
you can forget that.

00:17:52.306 --> 00:17:55.723
You can forget what's the pi root theory.

00:17:56.803 --> 00:17:59.392
You could forget the square root of 181.

00:17:59.392 --> 00:18:02.872
You can forget the square
root of 81, that's knowledge.

00:18:02.872 --> 00:18:04.282
- Come on, now, that's--

00:18:04.282 --> 00:18:05.282
- That's the back?

00:18:05.282 --> 00:18:06.428
- Yeah, that's the back.

00:18:06.428 --> 00:18:09.404
(audience laughing)

00:18:09.404 --> 00:18:10.402
